  "text": "Iqa‘ Zaffa 4/4 Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Zaffa Iqa‘ Zaffa is named after a wedding procession involving a loud and diverse group of percussion instruments. Aside from weddings, it is a possible modulation from slowed down versions of 4/4 iqa‘at like Baladi and Maqsum . Duqqu il-Mazahir (1952) Vocals and Music by Farid al-Atrash Alf Leila w Leila (1969) Umm Kulthum Music by Baligh Hamdi (Egypt) Qadd Ah Ya Hilu Muhammad Khayri Qadd Ya Mal il-Sham Sabah Fakhri Music by Ahmad Abu Khalil al-Qabbani Hann el-Hadid (1974) Joseph Saqr Music by Ziad Rahbani From the musical Nazl el-Surur Iqa‘ Zaffa 4/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
